{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:Observations.EosBorromeanCfl","@type":"LeanModule","name":"Observations.EosBorromeanCfl","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.cs_borromean_nonrelativistic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.cs_borromean_nonrelativistic","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/eos-borromean-cfl.lean#L92-L110","doc":"At nuclear saturation density, E_F ≪ M_B, so c_s² ≪ 1.\nWe show: for any E_F < M_B/100, c_s² < 1/100. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.cs_squared_borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.cs_squared_borromean","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/eos-borromean-cfl.lean#L86-L90","doc":"Speed of sound in the Borromean phase at Fermi energy E_F.\nc_s² = (2/3) · E_F / (M_B + E_F). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.conformal_cs_squared","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.conformal_cs_squared","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/eos-borromean-cfl.lean#L82-L84","doc":"The conformal speed of sound squared. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.mass_ratio_gt_1000","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.mass_ratio_gt_1000","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/eos-borromean-cfl.lean#L75-L80","doc":"The mass ratio M_B/M_D exceeds 1000 at q = 1.1097. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.M_D_small","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.M_D_small","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/eos-borromean-cfl.lean#L69-L73","doc":"At q = 1.1097, M_D is small. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.M_B_large","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.M_B_large","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/eos-borromean-cfl.lean#L63-L67","doc":"At q = 1.1097, M_B is large. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.stiffness_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.stiffness_ratio","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/eos-borromean-cfl.lean#L57-L61","doc":"The stiffness ratio P_D/P_B at equal baryon density.\nDominated by M_B/M_D × 3^{2/3}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.pressure_coeff_cfl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.pressure_coeff_cfl","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/eos-borromean-cfl.lean#L54-L55","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.pressure_coeff_borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.pressure_coeff_borromean","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/eos-borromean-cfl.lean#L47-L52","doc":"Fermi gas pressure for baryons at number density n_B.\nP = ℏ_q² (3π²)^{2/3} / (5M) · n_B^{5/3}\nWe factor out n_B^{5/3} and define the pressure coefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.M_D","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.M_D","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/eos-borromean-cfl.lean#L41-L45","doc":"Effective quark mass in the CFL phase (crossing energy per quark).\nThree quarks per baryon, each with crossing energy from the\nHopf link.  Vol(L_H) = 0, so no volume contribution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.M_B","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.M_B","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/eos-borromean-cfl.lean#L37-L39","doc":"Baryon mass in the Borromean phase (topological mass formula). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/eos-borromean-cfl.lean#L33-L35","doc":"The q-deformed Planck constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.V_B'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.V_B'","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/eos-borromean-cfl.lean#L29-L31","doc":"Borromean volume (8 × Catalan's constant). ","signatureChunk":0}]}